# Anusim — Project Overview

## What this app is
Anusim (ענוסים — Hebrew for "forced ones") is a Next.js web application currently in early development. Domain logic is not yet built; the codebase is a clean scaffold.

## Tech Stack

| Layer | Technology |
|---|---|
| Framework | Next.js 16 — App Router |
| Language | TypeScript 5 |
| UI | React 19 |
| Styling | Tailwind CSS v4 |
| Linting | ESLint 9 |

## Folder Structure

```
src/
└── app/
    ├── layout.tsx          # Root layout (metadata, global styles)
    ├── page.tsx            # Home page
    ├── globals.css         # Global styles — only `@import "tailwindcss"`
    ├── pages/              # UI page routes (App Router)
    │   └── [route]/
    │       └── page.tsx
    └── api/                # API route handlers
        └── [route]/
            └── route.ts
```

## Path Alias
`@/*` maps to `src/*` — always use it for imports (never relative `../../`).

## Key Conventions
- All new pages go under `src/app/pages/[name]/page.tsx`
- All new API routes go under `src/app/api/[name]/route.ts`
- Keep `globals.css` minimal — use Tailwind utility classes instead
